    "supported": "The official process-control guard can prevent terminating multiprocessing.Pool workers in both unchanged-package images. Busy-exit controls time out in 6/6 guarded and 0/6 unguarded cases; quick-map controls time out in 1/6 guarded and 0/6 unguarded cases. Completed map work can usually exit naturally despite denied kill requests, but one original-image repeat also hung after the map completed.",
